{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner: what the woo project's Durable Object write storms teach Artroom (hugh, 2026-10-02: be cautious, having been burnt). Sources: woo commits 6d2c425a and 50163fc1 (2026-08-02, the billing gate), 3f6e5a29 and f4b5dbaf (2026-07-28, the reply-cache and observation-act fixes), spec/operations/net-cutover.md and observability.md. Lessons: (1) the Cloudflare billing API is the only authority for physical rows written; application metrics cannot reconstruct base-table plus secondary-index writes, so woo attributes rows per namespace and per object from the billing datasets and fails closed on incomplete data. (2) Storms came from fan-out writes across objects, from retries and concurrent reads each minting a durable row, from unbounded caches inside a window that never expires, from startup write amplification on cold init, and from a hot object's roster growing without bound; the fixes were receipts without head advance, FIFO quotas with insert and prune in one transaction, dedup of no-op writes, per-turn budgets refused by name, and a load-time gate of 250,000 total rows and 50,000 per object. Artroom's shapes that match: every setAlarm is a row write and nextAlarm runs on every commit (core.ts committed at eight sites) and on the five-second loop; the entries table carries six secondary indexes in room/src/store.ts so one act is several physical rows; attention fans out one row per principal per item (core.ts:859) with no cap and no pruning, which is woo's roster-growth shape if a notify rule targets a large team; idem rows are written for every act and never pruned (admission.ts:1493, 1510); policy activation recomputes every open proposal and every landing resets every open preview, which is woo's fan-out shape; createSchema and eight migrations run on every new object. Applied as conditions: request 99782949 gains FIFO caps on attention and idem with insert-and-prune in one transaction and a per-item cap on attention fan-out; request d2cb872f gains a rows-written gate from the billing API, per namespace and per object, in the spike smoke run and as a scheduled alert, fail-closed, following woo's scripts/cloudflare-do-storage.ts; and a new request measures physical rows per act kind, per alarm tick and per publication before the durable deployment J2."}